Cross-finding analysis: adverse selection is constant, the close minute is not

Autonomous study of how every finding in this project interlocks, whether any
are orthogonal, and whether any combination beats its parts.

1. ALMOST EVERYTHING IS ONE FINDING

Pairwise correlation across 8,200 in-band markets is ~0 for every signal
(max 0.181). Only two carry an effect:

  no-fill      +20.96pp standalone
  minute :00    +3.25pp standalone,  +3.37pp conditional on no-fill
  calm / tight / cheap / side   noise

no-fill and :00 are uncorrelated (r = -0.003) and each survives conditioning
on the other. That orthogonality is the only reason a combination is worth
anything.

2. THE BIG NEGATIVE - FILL BIAS DOES NOT VARY

Tested whether adverse selection - the binding constraint on everything - is
weaker anywhere. Searched on TRAIN only, froze the winner, evaluated held-out.

  filled-cohort edge across every dimension:  -2.24c to -7.88c
  no-fill gap across every dimension:         +16.0pp to +24.4pp
  best train cell (XRP, -2.24c) -> valid -6.78c, test -6.87c
  held out CI [-12.31, -1.34]  P(<=0) 0.9918

It reverses completely out of sample. There is no regime where the
counterparty knows less. This EXPLAINS the thirteen prior failures rather than
merely adding a fourteenth: they all searched inside a space where the binding
constraint is constant, so anything they found was noise around a fixed drag.

3. THE SURVIVING PATTERN - THE MARKET DOES NOT PRICE THE CLOSE MINUTE

  minute   n    mean ask   win rate   implied-actual
   :00    277    0.7615     0.8448       +8.32pp
   :15    329    0.7605     0.7477       -1.28pp
   :30    278    0.7551     0.7698       +1.47pp
   :45    290    0.7613     0.7966       +3.53pp

The ask is identical across minutes. The win rate is not. That is a pricing
failure, not a cheaper price.

  :00 AND no-fill   n= 277  +6.32c  CI [+2.33, +10.33]  P(<=0) 0.0013
  :00 regardless    n= 963  +3.37c  CI [+0.03,  +6.80]  P(<=0) 0.0244
  other minutes     n=3095  -1.49c  CI [-3.78,  +0.77]  P(<=0) 0.9024

The probe adds +4.14c at :00 against +0.86c elsewhere - a real interaction of
+3.28c, not two effects summed.

SURVIVED: held-out only +5.43c P=0.0240 (lower bound above zero); day-matched
within-day +9.71c P=0.0003; selection correction over the four minutes
P=0.0158; leave-one-coin-out and leave-one-week-out all positive; dropping the
best five markets still +5.89c; proxy accuracy comparable across minutes
(0.7250-0.7632) so the contrast is not a classification artifact.

FAILED: hostile proxy stress. If the fill proxy is wrong on the best 25% the
(A) edge goes to -0.07c.

4. THE PROXY-FREE VERSION IS THE IMPORTANT ONE

(C) ":00 regardless of fill state" needs no probe, no fill model and no proxy.
+3.37c, P=0.0244, 13.1 commits/day held-out, ~$4.30/day at q15 - more per day
than the probe version despite being weaker per contract, and resting on far
less inference.

5. THIS SOFTENS THE EARLIER VERDICT

"No measurable edge anywhere" was too strong. It was reached by testing
POLICIES rather than testing PRICING. The right question was the one the
market answers badly: it quotes all four close minutes identically when they
do not behave identically.

NOT GLOSSED: the (C) lower bound is +0.03c, clearing zero by a hair; :00 has
been revisited several times so these tests are not mutually independent; no
mechanism is established, only a story about the top of the hour; and the
account must still be funded above $211.

NEXT TEST IS NOT MORE HISTORY. Run (C) forward at q5 on :00 only - one
eligibility line, no new architecture. 13 commits/day gives ~390 out-of-sample
observations in a month.

139 tests still pass.

